{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Mass.ColorTubeSpectralBridge","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Mass.ColorTubeSpectralBridge","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Ring.Defs","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Ring","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.LinearCombination"],"declarations":30,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.ColorTubeSpectralBridge.constraints_spectral_form","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.ColorTubeSpectralBridge.constraints_spectral_form","kind":"theorem","line":284,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/ColorTubeSpectralBridge.lean#L284-L296","doc":"**All three constraints are `z`-free in spectral coordinates.** Packaging the\nabove: each tube-chart equation equals a spectral invariant with no residual `z`.\nSo in the `wₖ` the Bring constraint system reads `S − zD = 0`, `H₂(w) = 0`,\n`H₃(w) = 0` — the `z`-dependence visible in the tube chart is entirely a shift\nartifact. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.ColorTubeSpectralBridge.spacetime_recovery_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.ColorTubeSpectralBridge.spacetime_recovery_eq","kind":"theorem","line":276,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/ColorTubeSpectralBridge.lean#L276-L282","doc":"**Spacetime recovery is `S − zD`, exactly.** Using the block's identities\n`χ_ζ(c) = D + z` and `p₁(c) = S − 4z`, the equation\n`z² − (χ_ζ(c) − 4)z + p₁(c)` reduces to `S − z·D` — i.e. the constraint is\nprecisely `z = S/D`, the block's own `eq:z-from-SD`. Stated on the spectral\naggregates `S`, `D` (no `ζ` needed: it enters only through `D`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.ColorTubeSpectralBridge.shifted_cubic_eq_H3","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.ColorTubeSpectralBridge.shifted_cubic_eq_H3","kind":"theorem","line":266,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/ColorTubeSpectralBridge.lean#L266-L274","doc":"**Shifted cubic is `H₃(w)`, exactly.** The block's\n`h₃(c) + z(p₁(c)² − 2h₂(c)) + 3z²p₁(c) + 4z³` equals the spectral Hermitian\ncubic `H₃(w)`; again every `z` cancels, so the constraint reads `H₃(w) = 0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.ColorTubeSpectralBridge.shifted_quadric_eq_H2","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.ColorTubeSpectralBridge.shifted_quadric_eq_H2","kind":"theorem","line":259,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/ColorTubeSpectralBridge.lean#L259-L264","doc":"**Shifted quadric is `H₂(w)`, exactly.** The block's\n`h₂(c) + z·p₁(c) + 2z² ` equals the spectral Hermitian quadric `H₂(w)` — all\n`z`-dependence cancels identically, so the constraint reads `H₂(w) = 0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.ColorTubeSpectralBridge.p1c_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.ColorTubeSpectralBridge.p1c_eq","kind":"theorem","line":254,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/ColorTubeSpectralBridge.lean#L254-L257","doc":"**`p₁(c) = S − 4z`** — the block's own shift identity, derived. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.ColorTubeSpectralBridge.h3c","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.ColorTubeSpectralBridge.h3c","kind":"def","line":249,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/ColorTubeSpectralBridge.lean#L249-L252","doc":"Tube-chart Hermitian cubic `h₃(c) = σ²c_g + c_b²c_r + c_r²σ + c_g²c_b`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.ColorTubeSpectralBridge.h2c","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.ColorTubeSpectralBridge.h2c","kind":"def","line":246,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/ColorTubeSpectralBridge.lean#L246-L247","doc":"Tube-chart Hermitian quadric `h₂(c) = σ·c_b + c_r·c_g`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.ColorTubeSpectralBridge.p1c","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.ColorTubeSpectralBridge.p1c","kind":"def","line":243,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/ColorTubeSpectralBridge.lean#L243-L244","doc":"Tube-chart first power sum `p₁(c)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.ColorTubeSpectralBridge.H3","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.ColorTubeSpectralBridge.H3","kind":"def","line":239,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/ColorTubeSpectralBridge.lean#L239-L241","doc":"Spectral Hermitian cubic `H₃(w) = w₁²w₃ + w₂²w₁ + w₄²w₂ + w₃²w₄`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.ColorTubeSpectralBridge.H2","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.ColorTubeSpectralBridge.H2","kind":"def","line":236,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/ColorTubeSpectralBridge.lean#L236-L237","doc":"Spectral Hermitian quadric `H₂(w) = w₁w₄ + w₂w₃` (pairs `wₖ` with `w₅₋ₖ`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.ColorTubeSpectralBridge.tube_psum3_of_bring","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.ColorTubeSpectralBridge.tube_psum3_of_bring","kind":"theorem","line":202,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/ColorTubeSpectralBridge.lean#L202-L213","doc":"**Tube-chart `p₃` is forced.** The spectral constraints `p₁ = p₂ = p₃ = 0`\nforce `p₃(c) = −5z³`. Together with the two lemmas above this is the complete\n`spectral ⇒ tube` transport of Bring's surface: `pₘ(c) = (−1)ᵐ·5·zᵐ`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.ColorTubeSpectralBridge.tube_psum2_of_bring","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.ColorTubeSpectralBridge.tube_psum2_of_bring","kind":"theorem","line":192,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/ColorTubeSpectralBridge.lean#L192-L200","doc":"**Tube-chart `p₂` is forced.** The spectral constraints `p₁(w) = p₂(w) = 0`\nforce `p₂(c) = 5z²` — the `z`-dependence is entirely a shift artifact. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.ColorTubeSpectralBridge.tube_psum1_of_bring","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.ColorTubeSpectralBridge.tube_psum1_of_bring","kind":"theorem","line":185,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/ColorTubeSpectralBridge.lean#L185-L190","doc":"**Tube-chart `p₁` is forced.** The spectral constraint `p₁(w) = 0` forces\n`p₁(c) = −5z` in the tube chart. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.ColorTubeSpectralBridge.psum3_shift","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.ColorTubeSpectralBridge.psum3_shift","kind":"theorem","line":178,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/ColorTubeSpectralBridge.lean#L178-L183","doc":"**Shift law for `p₃`.** `p₃(w) = p₃(c) + 3z·p₂(c) + 3z²·p₁(c) + 5z³`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.ColorTubeSpectralBridge.psum2_shift","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.ColorTubeSpectralBridge.psum2_shift","kind":"theorem","line":172,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/ColorTubeSpectralBridge.lean#L172-L176","doc":"**Shift law for `p₂`.** `p₂(w) = p₂(c) + 2z·p₁(c) + 5z²`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.ColorTubeSpectralBridge.psum1_shift","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.ColorTubeSpectralBridge.psum1_shift","kind":"theorem","line":166,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/ColorTubeSpectralBridge.lean#L166-L170","doc":"**Shift law for `p₁`.** `p₁(w) = p₁(c) + 5z` when `wₖ = cₖ + z`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.ColorTubeSpectralBridge.psum3","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.ColorTubeSpectralBridge.psum3","kind":"def","line":162,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/ColorTubeSpectralBridge.lean#L162-L164","doc":"Power sum `p₃` over the five spectral coordinates. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.ColorTubeSpectralBridge.psum2","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.ColorTubeSpectralBridge.psum2","kind":"def","line":158,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/ColorTubeSpectralBridge.lean#L158-L160","doc":"Power sum `p₂` over the five spectral coordinates. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.ColorTubeSpectralBridge.psum1","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.ColorTubeSpectralBridge.psum1","kind":"def","line":155,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/ColorTubeSpectralBridge.lean#L155-L156","doc":"Power sum `p₁` over the five spectral coordinates. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.ColorTubeSpectralBridge.tube_vieta_product","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.ColorTubeSpectralBridge.tube_vieta_product","kind":"theorem","line":127,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/ColorTubeSpectralBridge.lean#L127-L134","doc":"**Tube Vieta product is derived.** With all three spectral symmetric values,\nthe shift gives the block's `∏cᵢ = −(4z³+3z²+2z+1)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.ColorTubeSpectralBridge.tube_vieta_pair","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.ColorTubeSpectralBridge.tube_vieta_pair","kind":"theorem","line":118,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/ColorTubeSpectralBridge.lean#L118-L125","doc":"**Tube Vieta pair-sum is derived.** With the spectral values `Σwᵢ = −(z+1)`\nand `Σ_{i<j}wᵢwⱼ = z²+z+1`, the shift gives the block's `6z²+3z+1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.ColorTubeSpectralBridge.tube_vieta_sum","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.ColorTubeSpectralBridge.tube_vieta_sum","kind":"theorem","line":112,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/ColorTubeSpectralBridge.lean#L112-L116","doc":"**Tube Vieta sum is derived.** With the spectral value `Σwᵢ = −(z+1)`, the\nshift gives the block's `Σcᵢ = −(4z+1)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.ColorTubeSpectralBridge.esym3_shift","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.ColorTubeSpectralBridge.esym3_shift","kind":"theorem","line":105,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/ColorTubeSpectralBridge.lean#L105-L110","doc":"Generic shift identity for the third symmetric function. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.ColorTubeSpectralBridge.esym2_shift","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.ColorTubeSpectralBridge.esym2_shift","kind":"theorem","line":99,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/ColorTubeSpectralBridge.lean#L99-L103","doc":"Generic shift identity for the second symmetric function. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.ColorTubeSpectralBridge.esym1_shift","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.ColorTubeSpectralBridge.esym1_shift","kind":"theorem","line":95,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/ColorTubeSpectralBridge.lean#L95-L97","doc":"Generic shift identity for the first symmetric function. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.ColorTubeSpectralBridge.spectral_root_iff_tube_root","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.ColorTubeSpectralBridge.spectral_root_iff_tube_root","kind":"theorem","line":81,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/ColorTubeSpectralBridge.lean#L81-L85","doc":"**Root correspondence.** `w` is a root of the spectral cubic iff `w − z` is a\nroot of the tube cubic — the statement `cᵢ = wᵢ − z` at the level of roots. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.ColorTubeSpectralBridge.spectralCubic_eq_tubeCubic_shift","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.ColorTubeSpectralBridge.spectralCubic_eq_tubeCubic_shift","kind":"theorem","line":75,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/ColorTubeSpectralBridge.lean#L75-L79","doc":"The reverse reading: the spectral cubic is the tube cubic in `X − z`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.ColorTubeSpectralBridge.tubeCubic_eq_spectralCubic_shift","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.ColorTubeSpectralBridge.tubeCubic_eq_spectralCubic_shift","kind":"theorem","line":67,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/ColorTubeSpectralBridge.lean#L67-L73","doc":"**The coordinate change (the block's prose claim, now machine-checked).**\nThe tube cubic is the spectral cubic in the shifted variable: `T_z(c) = C_z(c + z)`.\nEquivalently the tube coordinate is `c = X − z`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.ColorTubeSpectralBridge.tubeCubic","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.ColorTubeSpectralBridge.tubeCubic","kind":"def","line":61,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/ColorTubeSpectralBridge.lean#L61-L65","doc":"The **color tube cubic** `T_z(c) = c³ + (4z+1)c² + (6z²+3z+1)c + (4z³+3z²+2z+1)`,\nas stated in the `color-tube-cubic` content block. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.ColorTubeSpectralBridge.spectralCubic","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.ColorTubeSpectralBridge.spectralCubic","kind":"def","line":55,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/ColorTubeSpectralBridge.lean#L55-L59","doc":"The **color spectral cubic** `C_z(X) = X³ + (z+1)X² + (z²+z+1)X + (z³+z²+z+1)`,\nmatching `QOU.Mass.ColorSpectralCubicGeometry`'s coefficients and the\n`e₁, e₂, e₃` of `QOU.Mass.ColorCubicPowerSums`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}